# Everything here is either a secret, a local artefact, or something the
# image rebuilds itself. Anything not excluded is uploaded to the Docker
# daemon on every build, so this file is a build-speed setting as well as a
# security one.
#
# ⚠ PATTERNS ARE MATCHED FROM THE CONTEXT ROOT, NOT AT EVERY LEVEL. A bare
# `.env` here would exclude `server/.env` — a file that does not exist — and
# happily copy `server/glaze/.env`, which is the one holding the secret key,
# the database password and the Gmail app password. Hence `**/` on everything
# that can appear at depth. An image layer is readable by anyone who can pull
# the image, and a secret in one cannot be deleted afterwards, only rotated.

# ---- Secrets ----
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# ---- Local artefacts ----
# The virtualenv: Windows binaries, useless in a Linux container, ~200 MB.
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Local database and uploaded media. Media lives in a named volume in
# production; copying a local copy in would shadow the volume's mount point.
**/db.sqlite3
**/db.sqlite3-journal
**/media/
**/staticfiles/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.log
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.DS_Store
